 "historical_through": "2025-26",
 "note": "Which sheet supplied each season, and what the boundary between them left to the tab. The historical tab is authoritative for every season it holds and the two forward-looking sheets are read only past it, so the boundary is the newest season on the tab rather than a year written into the code: the owner adding a season moves it. cutover lists, per forward sheet and per season it no longer answers for, the player-seasons and dollars that sheet still offers and how many of them the tab holds under the same name. A season well before the boundary may never have been read from that sheet by any build; the boundary season itself is the one that moved. Anything under missing_from_the_historical_tab the tab does not hold at all, and is the thing to look at before trusting a rollover.",
